# Tessera stdlib: the correctly rounded hyperbolic sine of B64
#
# For |x| < 1/4 an odd polynomial, checked with an error bound and redone in double-double when the bound
# can't decide the rounding. Otherwise sinh x = (e^|x| - e^-|x|) / 2 with both exponentials from the tables
# and polynomial of HypShared.te (e^-|x| is dropped past |x| ~ 36.7), again checked with an error bound.
# The accurate path evaluates the exponentials in double-double and looks the few hardest arguments up in a
# table of exact values.
# Round to nearest only: overflow gives a signed infinity, NaN comes back quiet, ±0 map to themselves.
#
# Ported from CORE-MATH, src/binary64/sinh/sinh.c via RazorForge's B64Sinh.rf.
# Copyright (c) 2023-2026 Alexei Sibidanov and Paul Zimmermann
# MIT license: see LICENSE-CORE-MATH

module Standard/System/Numerics/B64

### Hard-to-round arguments |x| (sorted), as B64 bits.
secret preset CM_B64_SINH_DB_X: &Array[U64, 51] <- [0x3FD364303E1AD8F6, 0x3FD4169F234F23B9,
    0x3FD616CC75D49226, 0x3FDAE3773250E7D2, 0x3FDB7EFA91915C95, 0x3FDD68039861AB53,
